# rm498, the tide's doorstop (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm498
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rm_dirk_rainmore
written_by codex
title the tide's doorstop
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk reads_floodwater_by_the_colour_of_a_threshold
likes pickled_herring dice new_boots thunder
dislikes deep_mud rats
fears a_stranger_turned_out_in_a_flood
hopes dry_boots_for_every_crossing
topics weather +0.6 friends +0.4 family +0.3
styles comfort=warm gossip=plain refuse=gentle tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps a wedge within reach, reads floodwater by the colour of a threshold, and sends wet travellers towards a seat without asking what the journey cost.

words
oath! = Soak my good soles | Wedge my supper sideways
saying! = Let the wet arrive first | A welcome needs dry boards
wedge = a cedar wedge | a bit of bevelled wood
tidebead = a brown bead of water | a shining brown drop
solehide = a new boot sole | a clean piece of leather
bootrag = a soft square of rag | a folded heel cloth
herringedge = a silver strip of herring | a sour sliver of fish
doorgap = a strip of daylight | a thumb of open space
watersill = a stained stone lip | a brown high-water line
seamwax = a lump of yellow wax | some soft boot wax
anklemark = a wet ring of fur | a dark band above the heel
doorbell = a hollow clapper | a bright little bell
ratboard = a stout low board | a piece of sound pine

grown
opinion @1 newcomers for 2 : A tired arrival won't know which paving stone tips. Give the directions before somebody's good boot fills up.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : I approve when a customer gets a patch of shelter before being asked the size of a purse.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : Bread under cover has fed a good many wet wolves who couldn't have managed both the loaf and the weather outdoors.
opinion @1 city for 1 : I know where each puddle begins. A town where I had to learn all those hollows afresh would tire me out.
opinion @1 road against 1 : Ask about the return in daylight. A dry crossing can disappear between a morning errand and an evening homecoming.
line @1 greet : In with you. I can move the wet things over.
line @1 greet.return : There's a dry bit left where we were speaking.
line @1 farewell : Mind where the little brown stream leaves the paving stones.
line @1 farewell.return : Good ground and an easy hinge to you.
line @1 react.news : Come in range. The dripping will swallow a quiet syllable.
line @1 react.news.new : That came across a sill I hadn't been minding.
line @1 react.news.known : I've heard the bell give that particular note before.
line @1 react.news.doubt : There's enough daylight under that tale to slide a wedge through.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : I'd wear a new sole out early to deliver that gladly.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Draw a seat nearer. News like that leaves a wolf slack at the knees.
line @1 ask.how : What sort of ground did your morning give you?
line @1 answer.how : Feet tired, heart reasonably dry. Glad enough of the company.
line @1 thank : You saved me the trouble of stooping for the wedge.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I've been the wet visitor often enough myself.
line @1 sympathise : There's a place to wring out your cuffs in private.
line @1 decline : I can't hold that open and still keep my footing here.
line @1 accept_decline : I'll take the pressure off that hinge, then.
line @1 reassure : Sit until the worst of the dripping's behind you.
line @1 ack : I heard you clearly across the boards.
scene work_1
when topic=work self.trade_words
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #self.trade_words.capitalize#, today. I watch feet when it rains.
b : Can you tell much from feet? | Do you watch them going out too?
a : I can tell who needs the stool before the trouble of speaking. | Especially then. A loose heel can slip on that first wet step.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather self.likes=thunder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : From a sound roof I enjoy the pause after the flash before the roof starts talking.
b : Do you count the pause? | Are you ever startled?
a : I count if somebody small wants a game of it. The storm keeps its own time. | Certainly. Enjoyment needn't be proof against jumping an inch.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like my herring sour enough to put the morning's wet out of my thoughts.
b : Does the skin stay on? | What goes beside it?
a : A little silver band does me nicely. It keeps the fish together till I've found my bread. | Something plain that won't argue with the pickle.

scene family_1
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd turn a dry cuff inside out for #self.spouse# if the last clean rag were needed.
b : Is a cuff big enough? | Wouldn't that spoil your sleeve?
a : For a pair of wet spectacles or a little decent comfort. I make no claims about mopping a floor. | Likely. I'd take that bargain quite cheerfully.

scene family_2
when topic=family self.parent=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I have thought of taking #self.child# on a walk just to find the dry crossings.
b : Why make a game of that? | Would the longer walk be worthwhile?
a : A child remembers the route that ends in fun long after the warning about wet feet has gone by. | The long one gives us a reason for stopping to look behind at the short one filling up.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wedge a door with the thin end barely showing.
b : So nobody trips? | How will the wedge come loose?
a : That, and I don't care to have a perfectly good visitor greet my wedge before greeting me. | Pull it clear after taking the door's weight in my hand. It needn't be a contest.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A boot lid makes a fair place to throw dice if the floor is full of puddles.
b : Won't they roll off? | What's a boot lid?
a : Put the lip upwards. A die wants very little persuading to stay if there's nowhere further to go. | The lid off a box that held my two new boots. Fine stout stuff.

scene animals_1
when topic=animals self.dislikes=rats
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I set #ratboard# in front of anything a rat might find worth tasting.
b : What about the smallest rats? | Do you trust a single board?
a : I look for daylight under the edge. A little daylight is a large invitation in some quarters. | Only to remind me to put the food away properly.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Brown water goes over the low stone first. It can look exactly like a solid road at dusk.
b : Where do your feet go? | Is there a sound to it?
a : The high side where I can still see a dry seam in the paving. | Listen for the trickle beneath the door lip. A proper stream gets there before you can judge its depth by sight.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : New boots feel most expensive immediately before the first deep puddle.
b : Would you go round? | Will the shine come back?
a : Several corners round, if I've enough time and a sound idea of what the next corner's doing. | Wax will manage most of it. I mind the cold water on the inside more than the colour outside.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When coin runs short I mend the heel before the wet finds it.
b : Can a wet one be saved? | Do you save the discarded hide?
a : Often, with time. It's losing the use of it while it dries that comes dear. | I keep a piece as thick as my thumb for a door that's begun to drag.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Every week I make enquiries about a petition that vanished inside the City Office.
b : What answer do you ask for? | Are you fed up with the walk?
a : Which room last had it. If the answer's always another room, I should at least like to know the shape of my journey. | The walk I understand. It's a dry piece of paper going missing indoors that wears me out.

scene gossip_1
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : What passed this way was that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : Did it come in from far? | Did you question the bearer?
a : Couldn't tell you. A report doesn't bring the mud of its whole road on its heels. | I asked how certain the account was. The answer didn't give me grounds to repeat it as settled.

story doorbell [topic=work]
  : I took a clapper out to polish it and laid it in a clean boot for safekeeping.
  : When I went looking for it there was a fine knock behind my own heel.
  b : Did someone want to come in?
  : My own boot did. I'd stepped in beside the clapper. We were both attending to business in very tight quarters.

story jarbone [topic=food]
  : I dropped one die into an empty pickle jar while putting away after supper.
  : It bounced round so long I had time to warm the heel of my bread.
  b : What number came up?
  : Six, looking down from above. Through the round glass there were dots enough to win six games.

story wedgetip [topic=memories]
  : I cut a wedge too thin and couldn't find it under the door the next morning.
  : A wet line crossed the boards and stopped dead at a dry triangle.
  b : Was that where you'd left it?
  : Precisely. The rain found my bit of wood without charging me for the information.

rule @wedge
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's my wedge. Give the wet boots room. | A dry stool should come before a question.

rule @thunder
when concept=bark self.likes=thunder
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wait for the answer from the roof beams. | That roll would carry well across a whole row of doors.

rule @heel
when concept=bark self.likes=new_boots
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's a shine worth keeping out of brown water. | Easy on the first step in good leather.

rule @dark
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Look for the last dry seam in the stones. | Can't judge that puddle by its reflection now.

dlg @1 resident.hub : You're welcome to let the damp out of your coat while we talk.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.trade_words] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I make sure a doubtful step doesn't send a customer home wet.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : This reached me in words clear enough to carry indoors. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Somebody going by had #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I didn't see where that started.
dlg @1 resident.bye : A level sill and warm socks when you reach home.
graft resident.hub
choice Can you tell which street will flood first? -> sill_brown
node sill_brown
say Find the door where a brown line crosses both jambs. Somebody spent a wet afternoon watching the water paint their threshold.
choice Is the way past that door still walkable? -> sill_dry
choice I'll watch where the reflection breaks. -> hub
node sill_dry
say Look for broken reflections. Dry stone splits a puddle into little pools. A single smooth reflection can hide a whole step.
choice I'll watch where the reflection breaks. -> hub


old
line @1 answer.how : Older knees. Very long acquaintance with the districts they'd sooner avoid in wet weather.
line @1 greet [here.time=dawn] : Early enough to choose a dry route before my knees choose for me.
scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My knees remember one low doorstep even when I come to it in the dark.
b : Does the stone feel familiar? | What if you come from the other side?
a : My leg gives a little lift that happens before I've thought to look. | Then I take my time. Old habits do fine work until somebody asks them to walk backwards.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I tire I sit with one boot drawn halfway off for the air.
b : Only the one? | Won't that crease the heel?
a : The other foot gets a turn when I'm sure I won't be called up immediately. | I slip my hand inside and ease the leather open. I've got as much time as the boot has.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Age has persuaded me to price new boots by the number of comfortable crossings.
b : How many do you expect? | What if they're too dear?
a : Enough that I forget which one was the first. Counting every blister makes a bad price seem worse. | I'd ask if my present pair can be resoled. They already know my feet.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : These days I feel grateful each time I have the strength to shift a stool for a wet arrival.
b : Can a visitor shift the stool? | Do you say anything with it?
a : Most can. I appreciate still being able to give the welcome with my own hands. | Sit, usually. The Bright One could make something very decent of a prayer as short as that.
